# .githooks/personal-patterns.local — OPTIONAL and GITIGNORED (CFG-869).
#
# Copy this file to .githooks/personal-patterns.local and list YOUR OWN identifiers.
# The pre-push guard sources it when present and blocks any push whose tracked text
# files carry one of them. leak-shapes.sh catches the CLASSES (a home directory, a
# hostname, an address, an e-mail); this file catches the VALUES a shape cannot: a
# name, a handle, an employer, a project codename, a NAS or printer name.
#
# Never commit the real file. It is exactly the list that must not be public, which
# is why it is not part of the template. The file is plain bash and is sourced.
#
# PERSONAL_PATTERNS — grep -E alternation, pipe-separated, in ONE pair of parentheses.
PERSONAL_PATTERNS='(Alice Example|alice\.example|example-corp|zebra-nas|DESKTOP-ABC1234)'

# PERSONAL_ALLOW — optional; grep -E over whole matching lines, to exempt a form you
# publish on purpose, such as the template's own clone URL.
PERSONAL_ALLOW='github\.com/alice-example/agent-fleet'
